# Generated F* extraction — regenerated by `./hax.sh extract` (and by the
# sha3-hax CI, which always re-extracts before verifying).  Do not commit
# these; only the hand-written Makefile in this directory is tracked.
# (Matches the policy already used by ml-kem, ml-dsa, aes, and kmac.)
*.fst
*.fsti

# Hand-written proof-helper modules (NOT generated by hax — they have no Rust
# source, so CI's re-extraction does not produce them).  They must be tracked
# or downstream modules fail with "module could not be resolved" (Error 72).
!Libcrux_sha3.Proof_utils.fst
!Libcrux_sha3.Proof_utils.Lemmas.fst
!Libcrux_sha3.Simd.Avx2.StoreBlockHelpers.fst
!Libcrux_sha3.Simd.Arm64.StoreBlockHelpers.fst

# Hand-written ABSTRACT interfaces for the SIMD incremental wrappers (`val
# t_KeccakState : Type0` + length-only posts).  These REPLACE the broken
# hax-generated concrete `.fsti` (dropped `noeq` + heavy `Simd.{Avx2,Arm64}`
# cone); the incremental modules are excluded from `--interfaces` so hax emits
# a transparent `.fst` these abstract over.  Restored in patch_fstar_extractions.
!Libcrux_sha3.Avx2.X4.Incremental.fsti
!Libcrux_sha3.Neon.X2.Incremental.fsti
